\title{Discrete Cube Root Assumption}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2026-01-15}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{The \em{discrete cube root assumption} (DCRA) says: for all polynomials #{P}, there is no algorithm that inputs #{N = pq} and #{f_N(x) = x^3 \bmod N} and outputs #{x} in time #{P(\log N)} with probability of correctness #{\geq \frac{1}{P(\log N)}}.}
